{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '-- prior closeout format --'\nsed -n '1,260p' ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF15-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '-- FF16/FF17 closeout format --'\nsed -n '1,180p' ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF16-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md\nsed -n '1,180p' ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF17-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '-- candidate target statements with exact context --'\nrg -n -C 3 'finiteRegionQubitAlgebraDirectedSystem|finiteRegionPartialTrace_(trans|comp|fullPauliRegionMatrix_dichotomy)|finiteRegionPartialTrace_regionDensity|localState_(localInclusion|comp_localInclusion|localInclusion_trans)|finiteRegionPartialTrace_regionDensity_trans' FiniteFiber/FullPauliDirectedLocalSystem.lean\"","aggregated_output":"-- prior closeout format --\n# FF15 live closeout adversarial review\n\n## Decision\n\n**Accepted at the packet's stated finite-region scope.**  The candidate\nmodule is byte-identical to the live\n`FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication.lean` and was reviewed only\nfrom the designated quarantine extraction.  The raw response archive remains\nat `FF15-finite-region-full-pauli-multiplication.tar.gz`; no archive build,\ndependency update, or dependency fetch was run.\n\n## Reviewed declarations and assumptions\n\n**Proved.**\n\n- `normalFormOneSiteMatrix_mul (p q : ProjectivePauliLabel)` proves the raw\n  one-site `X`-then-`Z` multiplication law with phase\n  `FullPauliWord.phaseEmbed ((p i).2 * (q i).1)`.\n- `finiteRegionNormalFormMatrix_mul (F) (p q)` proves finite-region projective\n  multiplication with the summed `finiteRegionNormalFormCocycle F p q`.\n- `cocycle_eq_finiteRegionNormalFormCocycle (F) (u v) (hu : u.support ⊆ F)`\n  identifies that exponent with `FullPauliWord.cocycle u v`.\n- `fullPauliRegionMatrix_mul (F) (a b) (ha : a.label.support ⊆ F)` proves\n  `fullPauliRegionMatrix F (a * b) = fullPauliRegionMatrix F a *\n  fullPauliRegionMatrix F b`.  Only the left support premise is needed by the\n  ordered cocycle, so this includes the requested local-local case.\n- `fullPauliRegionMatrix_one` and\n  `fullPauliRegionMatrix_negativeIdentity` give the identity and central\n  negative-identity cases.\n\n**Partial.**  The result is a finite-region operator identity only: no\nsupport/local-algebra identification, multi-region representation, colimit,\nnorm closure, state, GNS, or finite-fiber conclusion is claimed.\n\n**Blocked.**  No obstruction remains for FF15 itself.\n\n**Failed.**  No failed declaration or verification check.  A stdin-only\npretty-printing diagnostic was unavailable; it did not affect builds or\naxiom audits.\n\n## Adversarial findings\n\nNo confirmed defect in the reviewed scope.\n\n- The phase convention is preserved: the proof uses the existing\n  `FullPauliWord.phaseEmbed` and cocycle, while its imports retain the checked\n  one-site `X Z = -iY` convention.\n- The theorem's one-sided support condition is explicit and is not misreported\n  as a support/local-algebra equivalence.\n- The candidate module and audit contain no `sorry`, `admit`, project `axiom`,\n  `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration.\n- Remote README, handoff, summary, manifest, and all other snapshot files were\n  not adopted.\n\n## Live checks\n\n- `lake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed (3,204 jobs), after importing the reviewed module from\n  umbrella `FiniteFiber.lean`.\n- `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean` — passed; the eight FF15 public\n  declarations report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- `lake env lean tests/FullPauliMultiplicationAxiomAudit.lean` — passed with\n  the same axiom set.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Residual risk and cleanup\n\nLean compilation and axiom audits establish the named finite-dimensional\ntheorems, not later bridges.  Pre-existing dirty/untracked material was\npreserved.  No commit, push, manuscript edit, or destructive cleanup occurred.\n-- FF16/FF17 closeout format --\n# FF16 live closeout adversarial review\n\n## Decision\n\n**Accepted at the packet's stated finite-infrastructure scope.** Aristotle task `a1684489-8deb-4f62-8f5a-a592570dd778` was downloaded only into the I004 response quarantine. The live `FiniteFiber/FullPauliSupportLocality.lean` is byte-identical to the reviewed candidate (SHA-256 `33c06ce8a574c76846b66765ffc311c113365e22ef0112bc30a10bd526d1368d`). No build, dependency update, or dependency fetch was run in the downloaded snapshot.\n\n## Reviewed declarations and assumptions\n\n**Proved.**\n\n- `FullPauliWord.SupportedIn a F := a.label.support ⊆ F` is the explicit finite support predicate. `FullPauliWord.HasFiniteRegionRealization a F` means that there is `A : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F` whose `finiteRegionEmbed` equals `fullPauliRegionMatrix F' a` for every finite enlargement `F ⊆ F'`.\n- `finiteRegionEmbed_fullPauliRegionMatrix (F) (F') (hFF') (a) (ha)` proves identity padding under the exact premise `ha : a.SupportedIn F`.\n- `supportedIn_of_finiteRegionEmbed_eq (F) (F') (hFF') (a) (hsupp) (A) (hA)` proves the converse under `hsupp : a.SupportedIn F'` and `hA : fullPauliRegionMatrix F' a = finiteRegionEmbed F F' hFF' A`. The ambient premise is necessary: support wholly outside inspected `F'` is invisible there.\n- `supportedIn_iff_hasFiniteRegionRealization (F) (a)` is the requested equivalence. Its reverse direction applies the preceding theorem to `F ∪ a.label.support`, so it does not silently discard outside support.\n- `eq_fullPauliRegionMatrix_of_realization (F) (a) (A) (hA)` proves uniqueness by evaluating the all-enlargements premise at `F` itself.\n\nSupporting compiled lemmas: `labelXBit_of_fst_eq_zero`, `labelXBit_of_fst_ne_zero`, `normalFormOneSiteMatrix_labelXBit_ne_zero`, `normalFormOneSiteMatrix_zero_zero_of_fst_eq_zero`, `normalFormOneSiteMatrix_one_one_of_pure_z`, `fullPauliRegionMatrix_apply`, `zmod4PhaseFactor_ne_zero`, `restrictLabel_eq_pad_of_supportedIn`, and `finiteRegionEmbed_self`.\n\n**Partial.** This is an equivalence between explicit word support and the stated finite-region realization predicate only. It does not prove global-algebra membership, multi-region coherence beyond supplied identity padding, a directed colimit, norm closure, state, GNS representation, normality, von Neumann-algebra result, or finite-fiber conclusion.\n\n**Blocked.** None at FF16 scope.\n\n**Failed.** None. The remote snapshot's `FiniteFiber.lean` import change, README edit, metadata, handoff, manuscript copy, and all other noncandidate files were rejected. Only the candidate module and raw quarantine records were retained.\n\n## Adversarial findings\n\nNo confirmed defect in the accepted scope.\n\n- The apparent one-region counterexample is excluded by `HasFiniteRegionRealization`, which quantifies over every finite enlargement; the proof explicitly uses `F ∪ a.label.support`.\n- The converse retains its necessary support-in-`F'` premise and does not identify syntactic support with an unspecified local/global algebra.\n- The proof's nonzero phase and one-site matrix arguments are over `ℂ`; its cancellation step is justified by the established nonzero matrix entry.\n- The candidate has no declaration headed by `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or `implemented_by`, and contains no `sorry`, `admit`, or `native_decide`.\n\n## Live checks\n\n- `lake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliSupportLocality` — passed.\n- `lake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication` — passed.\n- `lake build FiniteFiber` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed.\n- `lake env lean --stdin` with `#print axioms` for every FF16 public theorem — passed; each footprint is a subset of `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean` — passed.\n- Placeholder declaration scan and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Residual risk and cleanup\n\nLean compilation and axiom inspection validate the formal declarations and their stated assumptions; they do not establish later quasilocal/GNS/type bridges. The raw archive is `FF16-full-pauli-support-locality.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `447389053d147319b70c0c519f027c25bfc78c085dcfca68c23e4b793345b727`, and the extracted remote project remains quarantined at `FF16-extracted/`. Pre-existing dirty and untracked project work was preserved. No manuscript edit, commit, push, or destructive cleanup occurred.\n# FF17 live closeout — full-Pauli stabilizer density\n\n**Decision: ACCEPTED at the packet's stated finite-volume scope.**\n\n## Quarantine and integration\n\n- Aristotle project: `a8623a7e-5752-4e4d-9667-d3c741247c1f`; completed task:\n  `44158f6b-4673-4e26-9871-9fc7717c0353`.\n- Raw archive retained at `FF17-full-pauli-stabilizer-density.tar.gz`, SHA-256\n  `7e86f988e2118b9e43141f319f65b9ccf5ae0802be34147d670212acdfc84a63`.\n- Complete dependency-free snapshot retained under `FF17-extracted/`; no Lake\n  command was run there.\n- Integrated only `FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean`.  Its live and\n  quarantined SHA-256 values agree:\n  `688162cc2779855e163f45fd210e4ddd36339579136fd3039f19df82cfca0a09`.\n- Rejected: the remote README attribution block, `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md`,\n  source-context/autonomy metadata, and the remote `manuscript/` copy.  No\n  manuscript or root import file was modified.\n\n## Proved\n\nFor `D : FullPauliRegionStabilizer Site`, the exact hypotheses are the fields\nat `FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean:303`: a subgroup of\n`FullPauliWord Site`, a finite `region`, an explicit `Fintype` on the subgroup,\nsupport containment for every group member, elementwise involutivity\n`g * g = 1`, and exclusion of `FullPauliWord.negativeIdentity`.\n\n- `FullPauliRegionStabilizer.stabilizerData` constructs\n  `FinitePauliStabilizerData D.group D.region.card`; the representation\n  injectivity and matrix `-1` exclusion are established internally, rather\n  than inserted as fields.\n- The packet's target identity is exactly\n  `FullPauliRegionStabilizer.regionToQubitMatrix_regionDensity`\n  (`FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean:477`): after the explicit basis\n  reindexing, the finite-region average\n  `((2 : C)^D.region.card)^(-1) * sum_g fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region g`\n  is `D.stabilizerData.stabilizerDensity`.\n- The exact normal-form convention is preserved by\n  `fullPauliRegionMatrix_eq_pauliSign_smul`: the central `ZMod 4` phase plus\n  the checked Hermitian correction produces the signed Pauli term used by the\n  finite-density layer.\n- Derived finite-volume conclusions are checked: projector invariance,\n  self-adjoint idempotence, trace formula, trace-one density,\n  trace-normalized-projector identity, positive semidefiniteness, and nonzero\n  projector (`:490`--`:539`).\n- `ofGlobalStabilizer` retains the added premises explicitly:\n  `hinv : forall g in S, g * g = 1` and `negativeIdentity notin S` (`:677`--`:688`).\n  `ofGenerators` discharges these only from the existing explicit\n  pairwise-commuting, order-two, consistent generator data; it does not infer\n  them from short-range order.\n\n## Partial\n\nThis accepts only the manuscript's finite-region density formula\n`rho_F = 2^(-|F|) sum_{g in G_{S,F}} g` and its finite matrix consequences.\nThe module does not prove region-to-region partial-trace compatibility, a\nquasilocal completion, a global state, GNS data, normality, or a finite-fiber/\ntype conclusion.  Those remain open and are not needed for FF17.\n\n## Blocked\n\nNone within the stated FF17 target.\n\n## Failed\n\nNone.  No target was silently weakened: the finite group, its support,\ninvolutivity, and consistency are all visible assumptions of the proved\nfinite-volume theorem.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo confirmed defect found.  The main potential scope failure—treating a\nfinite syntactic local group as a completed quasilocal construction—is avoided:\nthe only global-group constructor remains conditional and the source explicitly\ndisclaims every global-state/GNS claim.  The matrix identity is transported by\nan explicit basis algebra equivalence, not asserted by notation.\n\n## Live verification\n\nAll commands below were run in `formalization_finite_fibers`, never in the\nquarantine snapshot:\n\n```text\nlake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliStabilizerDensity                PASS\nlake build FiniteFiber.FinitePauliStabilizer                     PASS\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication      PASS\nlake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliSupportLocality                  PASS\nlake build FiniteFiber                                           PASS\nlake build                                                       PASS\nlake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean                              PASS\n```\n\nA direct generated `#print axioms` audit covered all 41 public FF17 theorems.\nEach reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.  A direct\nscan found no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or\n`implemented_by` token in the new module.\n-- candidate target statements with exact context --\n18-* **Local inclusions.**  The identity padding `A ↦ A ⊗ 1` given by\n19-  `finiteRegionEmbed F F' hFF'`, written `localInclusion hFF'` for the\n20-  order-indexed form.  The instance\n21:  `finiteRegionQubitAlgebraDirectedSystem` records that these satisfy the\n22-  identity and composition laws of a `DirectedSystem`.\n23-* **Actual full-Pauli images.**  The finite-region matrix\n24-  `fullPauliRegionMatrix F a` of an algebraic full-Pauli word.  For a word\n--\n40-* `trace_finiteRegionPartialTrace` and\n41-  `finiteRegionPartialTrace_mul_finiteRegionEmbed`: the partial trace preserves\n42-  the trace and is a module map for the local inclusion.\n43:* `finiteRegionPartialTrace_trans` / `finiteRegionPartialTrace_comp`: **the\n44-  composition law** of the finite restrictions, `Tr_{F' \\ F} ∘ Tr_{F'' \\ F'} =\n45-  Tr_{F'' \\ F}`.\n46:* `finiteRegionPartialTrace_fullPauliRegionMatrix_dichotomy`: the manuscript's\n47-  surviving-term dichotomy — a full-Pauli word survives the partial trace\n48-  exactly when it is already supported in the smaller region, and is then\n49-  rescaled by `2^{|F' \\ F|}`; otherwise its partial trace is `0`.\n50:* `FullPauliStabilizerSystem.finiteRegionPartialTrace_regionDensity`: the\n51-  manuscript's compatibility relation `ρ_F = Tr_{F' \\ F}(ρ_{F'})` for the actual\n52-  finite stabilizer densities.\n53:* `FullPauliStabilizerSystem.localState_localInclusion`: **the exact\n54-  finite-stage restriction formula** `ω_{F'}(A ⊗ 1_{F' \\ F}) = ω_F(A)` for the\n55-  finite local states `ω_F(A) = Tr(ρ_F A)`, with\n56:  `localState_localInclusion_trans` and\n57:  `finiteRegionPartialTrace_regionDensity_trans` its composition law.\n58-* `FullPauliStabilizerSystem.localState_fullPauliRegionMatrix`: each finite\n59-  local state is the stabilizer state of its region.\n60-* `zWordSystem`: the hypotheses are non-vacuous.\n--\n322-`F ⊆ F' ⊆ F''`, tracing out `F'' \\ F'` and then `F' \\ F` is exactly tracing\n323-out `F'' \\ F`.\n324--/\n325:theorem finiteRegionPartialTrace_trans (F F' F'' : Finset Site)\n326-    (hFF' : F ⊆ F') (hF'F'' : F' ⊆ F'') (A : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F'') :\n327-    finiteRegionPartialTrace F F' hFF'\n328-        (finiteRegionPartialTrace F' F'' hF'F'' A) =\n--\n350-    Fintype.sum_prod_type]\n351-\n352-/-- The composition law as an equality of linear maps. -/\n353:theorem finiteRegionPartialTrace_comp (F F' F'' : Finset Site)\n354-    (hFF' : F ⊆ F') (hF'F'' : F' ⊆ F'') :\n355-    (finiteRegionPartialTrace F F' hFF').comp\n356-        (finiteRegionPartialTrace F' F'' hF'F'') =\n357-      finiteRegionPartialTrace F F'' (hFF'.trans hF'F'') :=\n358:  LinearMap.ext fun A => finiteRegionPartialTrace_trans F F' F'' hFF' hF'F'' A\n359-\n360-/-! ### Partial traces of finite-region full-Pauli matrices -/\n361-\n--\n427-for the words already supported in `F`, and then it is the rescaled\n428-finite-region matrix on `F`.\n429--/\n430:theorem finiteRegionPartialTrace_fullPauliRegionMatrix_dichotomy\n431-    (F F' : Finset Site) (hFF' : F ⊆ F') (a : FullPauliWord Site)\n432-    (hsupp : a.SupportedIn F') :\n433-    (a.SupportedIn F ∧ finiteRegionPartialTrace F F' hFF' (fullPauliRegionMatrix F' a) =\n--\n462-the identity-padding inclusions satisfy the identity and composition laws of a\n463-directed system.\n464--/\n465:instance finiteRegionQubitAlgebraDirectedSystem :\n466-    DirectedSystem (fun F : Finset Site => finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F)\n467-      (fun _ _ h A => localInclusion h A) where\n468-  map_self := fun {F} A => finiteRegionEmbed_self F A\n--\n543-local density of `F`.  This is the manuscript's relation\n544-`ρ_F = Tr_{F' \\ F}(ρ_{F'})`.\n545--/\n546:theorem finiteRegionPartialTrace_regionDensity (F F' : Finset Site) (hFF' : F ⊆ F') :\n547-    finiteRegionPartialTrace F F' hFF' (S.regionDensity F') = S.regionDensity F := by\n548-  classical\n549-  have hle := S.regionStabilizer_group_mono F F' hFF'\n--\n607-the finite local state of `F'` restricted along the identity-padding inclusion\n608-is exactly the finite local state of `F`.\n609--/\n610:theorem localState_localInclusion (F F' : Finset Site) (hFF' : F ⊆ F')\n611-    (A : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F) :\n612-    S.localState F' (localInclusion hFF' A) = S.localState F A := by\n613-  rw [localState_apply, localState_apply, localInclusion_eq,\n614-    ← trace_finiteRegionPartialTrace F F' hFF',\n615-    finiteRegionPartialTrace_mul_finiteRegionEmbed,\n616:    S.finiteRegionPartialTrace_regionDensity F